Root cause:
The bug was caused by a double unlock of the global bitmap inode in the `ocfs2_reserve_cluster_bitmap_bits()` function when handling the error case after a retry. Specifically, if the function `ocfs2_try_to_free_truncate_log()` was called and it failed, the code attempted to unlock the inode again in the error handling branch without checking if it was already unlocked, leading to a potential double unlock scenario and resulting in a kernel BUG. This issue could also occur if the `ocfs2_inode_lock` function failed without needing a retry, further complicating the locking logic.
